The 1930 Gurmukhi text of Gurushabad Ratnakar Mahan Kosh
(Bhai Kahan Singh Nabha) is in the public domain.

Sikhi.io's own contributions to this compiled dataset (the Hindi text,
the machine translations, the JSON packaging, and the viewer in site/)
are released under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(CC BY 4.0).

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may use, share, and adapt those contributions, including
commercially, if you give appropriate credit.

NOT covered by CC BY 4.0: the English text (data/entries/en.json and
its derivatives) follows the English edition of the Mahan Kosh
published by Punjabi University, Patiala (2006–2011), which remains
under Punjabi University's copyright. It is included for
non-commercial study and research. For any other use, obtain
permission from Punjabi University, Patiala (Publication Bureau).
The machine translations are made from that English text, so the
same caution applies to them until their status is confirmed.

Suggested attribution:

  Mahan Kosh multilingual dataset, from Bhai Kahan Singh Nabha,
  Gurushabad Ratnakar Mahan Kosh (1930); English after Punjabi
  University Patiala (2006–2011), © Punjabi University, Patiala.
  Packaged by Sikhi.io (https://sikhi.io/dictionary), in honour of
  Guru Tegh Bahadur Ji.

Machine-translated languages have not been reviewed by native
speakers or subject scholars.
